   "unmapped": [
    "Abstract policy set Pi; guarantees adapt simultaneously to the number of changes L and the total amount of change Delta (both unknown); non-stationarity measure Delta is defined via the base algorithm's guarantee (Assumption 1)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "Ahead of time, the learner is given a policy set $\\Pi$, and the environment decides $T$ reward functions $f_1, \\ldots, f_T: \\Pi \\to [0,1]$ unknown to the learner. Then, in each round $t$, the learner chooses a policy $\\pi_t\\in\\Pi$ and receives a noisy reward $R_t \\in [0,1]$ whose mean is $f_t(\\pi_t)$. The dynamic regret of the learner is defined as $\\Regret = \\sum_{t=1}^T (f^\\star_t - R_t)$"
  },
